{"request_sha256": "a6ed5b9682f2fb6a462786aae1dc6133b5352735e9a81fdeb4df2cca1f8a513b", "prompt_sha256": "b977396bce80653bb49b01ba0711ae5f59325eab09c2c5a681f87fff43ab3911", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "8cd5dc8a88cce19d478a45d924476a4e4077e0a73c3125870a553a99c00a1f64", "schema_sha256": "4c13c160206ee1491a194676a627beccdc5e53d97adad294646e2d74ab3f74f5", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "failed_or_tools_or_unknown_usage_or_cardinality", "forbidden_tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 3900}, "answer": {"traits": [{"id": "T01-crown-pinnate-arching", "priority": "core", "observation": "Crown is a dense, roughly hemispherical rosette of long pinnate (feather) fronds radiating in all directions; upper fronds ascend stiffly, mid and lower fronds arch outward and recurve downward, giving a fountain silhouette wider than tall in reference-0 and strongly recurved frond tips in reference-1.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T02-trunk-diamond-leafbase-stubs", "priority": "core", "observation": "Trunk surface is covered in persistent cut/broken leaf-base stubs of squarish-to-diamond outline, arranged in intersecting spiral rows, projecting a few centimetres from the trunk and producing a coarse knobbly texture; visible at coarse scale in reference-0 and in sharp detail in reference-1 and reference-2.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T03-no-crownshaft", "priority": "core", "observation": "No smooth green crownshaft is present; the frond bases emerge directly from the rough stubbed trunk apex, with petiole bases visible as flattened tan/orange-brown straps in reference-1.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T04-pinnae-stiff-narrow-v-ranked", "priority": "core", "observation": "Leaflets are narrow, stiff, linear and sharply pointed, inserted along the rachis in several planes/angles rather than one flat plane, giving each frond a plumose or V-sectioned look; pinnae spacing is regular and dense toward the mid-rachis.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T05-foliage-color-grey-green-glaucous", "priority": "core", "observation": "Frond colour reads as muted grey-green to blue-green with a dull, waxy (non-glossy) surface in reference-1 and reference-2; in reference-0 the crown reads darker green, consistent with backlit dusk lighting.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T06-trunk-columnar-untapered", "priority": "core", "observation": "Trunk is a single unbranched column of near-constant diameter along its visible length, with a modest flare at ground contact in reference-0; no branching or forking anywhere.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T07-fruit-strands-pendent", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Two pendent infructescences hang from within the crown in reference-0, each on a stout arching orange-tan stalk bearing dense clusters of small ovoid orange-to-red fruits; the fruit mass hangs below the frond bases and is clearly separate from the foliage.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T08-dead-frond-skirt", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "A skirt of dead, brown, collapsed fronds hangs vertically beneath the living crown in reference-0, forming a ragged fringe between crown and bare trunk.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T09-trunk-fibrous-matting", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Between and behind the stubs the trunk shows coarse brown fibre, shredded husk and matted tissue filling the interstices; fibre tone ranges from pale tan to dark red-brown.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T10-petiole-bases-orange-tan", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Lower petiole/leaf-base straps at the crown are broad, flattened and pale tan-to-orange with darker margins, contrasting with the green of the blade; visible where fronds meet the trunk in reference-1.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T11-epiphytes-on-trunk", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Bright yellow-green ferns with narrow pinnate fronds grow out of the stub interstices over a broad band of the trunk, densest in a mid-trunk zone; also small vines/seedlings lower down. Observation only — whether this reflects trunk age, humidity, or management is not determinable from the images.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T12-crown-apex-spear", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "The crown centre shows a cluster of erect, still-unopened or newly opened central fronds forming a vertical spear-like core above the arching mature fronds.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T13-basal-pinnae-spines", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Near the proximal end of the petioles the pinnae appear reduced to short, stiff, spreading spine-like segments; resolution limits confirmation of true acanthophylls.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1"], "uncertain": true}, {"id": "T14-trunk-lean-curve", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Trunk posture varies: strongly leaning and S-curved from the ground with a thickened basal elbow in reference-0, versus essentially vertical and straight in reference-1 and reference-2.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T15-stub-retention-extent", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Extent of retained leaf-base stubs differs: reference-0 shows a worn, low-relief stubbed trunk with only shallow diamond patterning over most of its length, while reference-1 and reference-2 show deep, sharply projecting stubs over the entire visible column.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T16-fruiting-state", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Fruiting is present in reference-0 and absent from the visible crowns in reference-1; presence, colour stage and number of fruit strands are acceptable variation.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T17-crown-density-frond-count", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Crown fullness varies from a moderately open crown with visible gaps between fronds (reference-0) to a dense overlapping crown filling the frame (reference-1).", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T18-neighbouring-stems", "priority": "variation", "observation": "reference-1 includes at least one additional stubbed trunk and further crowns at frame edges; whether these are separate individuals or suckers of one clump cannot be determined.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1"], "uncertain": true}, {"id": "T19-ground-transition", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Ground contact is visible only in reference-0, where the trunk meets a grassy earth bank with a swollen, fibre-covered basal flare and no exposed stilt roots; no ground-level evidence exists in reference-1 or reference-2 despite the P-BASE view label.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": true}, {"id": "T20-trunk-colour-range", "priority": "variation", "observation": "Trunk colour ranges from uniform grey-brown weathered tone (reference-0) to warm red-brown with pale grey bleached stub faces (reference-1, reference-2); directional sunlight in the latter two accounts for part of the contrast.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}], "observations": ["Three references are treated as independent records; no assumption is made that they depict the same individual, site, or a sequence of change over time.", "View coverage is uneven: only reference-0 shows the whole plant, crown silhouette, fruit, and ground contact. reference-1 and reference-2 are both mid-trunk/crown-underside views at different magnifications; neither includes the stem base, so base-specific morphology (root mass, offshoots/suckers, soil interface) is unresolved.", "Recognition rests primarily on the combination of an unbranched stubbed trunk with diamond-patterned persistent leaf bases, absence of a crownshaft, and a full rosette of long arching pinnate grey-green fronds; fruit is diagnostic when present but is not required for recognition.", "Lighting and time of day differ markedly (backlit dusk with heavy cloud in reference-0; bright midday sun with blue sky in reference-1 and reference-2), so apparent foliage and trunk colour differences are confounded with illumination and should not be read as morphological differences.", "Fern growth on the trunk and the fibre matting are co-located in the stub interstices; this is recorded as an observation of what is visible. Candidate causes (moist climate, long stub retention, wind-borne spores) are not distinguishable from the images.", "The strong trunk lean and basal elbow in reference-0 is recorded as observed posture only; phototropism, bank subsidence, storm displacement, or sap-tapping practice are all possible and none is supported over the others by visible evidence.", "Scale cannot be measured reliably: no scale object is present in reference-1 or reference-2, and estimates in reference-0 depend on distant vegetation and structures of unknown size.", "Small structures near the petiole bases (possible spines) and the fine texture of individual pinnae margins are at or below the resolution limit in all three references and remain uncertain."]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"e949eb24-50ec-439e-